{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792832411,"nonce":"/BmFj1d2Xju/GDroaIo3rz2YJjc=","title":"sched: cancel the tasks a scope spawned","message":"ChimpMonk's editor previews a game (Play) and restores a baseline on Stop. Stop must drop every fiber and task the game's modules spawned, without snapshotting them; fibers there are for non-replay-critical behaviour.\n\nTasks can't be cancelled today. `wait::discard` drops a wait token, not a task.\n\nWanted:\n- A task scope (a module, or a world-level group a host opens) that the tasks spawned under it inherit.\n- `cancel(scope)`, which unwinds or abandons each task at its next park or resume, releases what it holds (wait registrations, host states, the stack), and never runs it again.\n\nEach language needs a defined behaviour for a cancelled fiber's pending frames: Haxe traps, Wren fibers, and Zyntax handler segments and HostTasks.","files":null}]}